Whether the path of an image, e.g. [1;94m![image path](tom&jerry.png)[0m (this path does not exist on purpose), is [3muri-escaped[0m depends on the output mode:
--html escapes, --ansi, --text and --tty (the text modes) do not, and the GUI viewer does when it loads the image from the path but does not on cursor hover: [1;93mimage path[0m [4;32m{tom&jerry}[0m.
The [3muri-escaping[0m rules for a link like [1;94m[link](https://tom&jerry.com)[0m (OK, the URL isn't quite valid), also depend on the output mode: --html escapes, text modes do not, the GUI viewer does on clicking the link but does not on cursor hover: [1;93mlink[0m [4;32m<https://tom&jerry.com>[0m.
